# Raffle / draw winner — an ExactOdds casino rule pack.
#
# Prize draws and raffle winners have to be provably fair the same way dice
# rolls are: a published seed, a published mixing rule, and a winner anyone
# can recompute. This program takes the draw seed and the ticket count and
# returns the winning ticket number — the same ticket on every seat, or the
# program refuses to compile.
#
# Rules: tickets are numbered 1..N; winner = 1 + state % tickets. Mixing is
# Park-Miller under 2^31 (the same arithmetic the dice game uses), so every
# seat — Python big-ints, C int64, JS doubles — computes the identical
# value. The seed must be a non-negative integer below 290 trillion and
# committed before ticket sales close — a seed chosen after the draw is not
# provably fair.

def raffle_winner(seed: int, tickets: int) -> int do
    mut mixed = (seed * 31 + 17) % 2147483647
    mut state = (48271 * mixed) % 2147483647
    ret 1 + state % tickets
end

# Audited cases.
say(raffle_winner(12345, 100))
say(raffle_winner(999, 50))
say(raffle_winner(1, 10))
